==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-hold forth.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|hold<,,held> forth}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[extend]] or [[offer]], [[propose]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To talk at great length.
#: {{syn|en|expatiate|harangue}}
#* {{RQ:Lawrence Sons and Lovers|chapter=5|passage=The girls all liked to hear him talk. They often gathered in a little circle while he sat on a bench, and '''held forth''' to them, laughing.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1918|author={{w|W. B. Maxwell}}|title=The Mirror and the Lamp|chapter=2|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL1097634W|passage={{...}}they did not like him coming round of an evening and drinking weak whisky-and-water while he '''held forth''' on railway debentures and corporation loans.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|title={{w|Cloud Atlas (novel)|Cloud Atlas}}|author=David Mitchell|authorlink=David Mitchell (author)|year_published=2012|isbn=9780345807472|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/cloudatlasnovel0000mitc_c5p2/page/55/mode/1up|page=55|passage=Warmed to the woman somewhat, I admit it. She '''holds forth''' like a man and smokes myrrhy cigarettes through a rhino-horn holder.}}

